language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ csplib_010_social_golfers_problem: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ The coordinator of a local golf club has n_groups * group_size golfers, each of whom plays golf once a week, always in n_groups groups of group_size golfers. Make a schedule of play for these golfers over n_weeks weeks, such that no golfer plays in the same group as any other golfer on more than one occasion.
$
$ Save this file as model.eprime. Download `csplib_010_social_golfers_problem.json` and `dcp_convert_essence.py` from the
$ problem's page:
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/csplib_010_social_golfers_problem.html
$ Convert the instances once, then run the first one with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the
$ solution is written to `csplib_010_social_golfers_problem_1.param.solution`:
$   python dcp_convert_essence.py csplib_010_social_golfers_problem.json
$   savilerow model.eprime csplib_010_social_golfers_problem_1.param -run-solver

$ n_groups: the number of groups each week
given n_groups : int(1..)
$ group_size: the number of golfers in each group
given group_size : int(1..)
$ n_weeks: the number of weeks
given n_weeks : int(1..)
$ the number of golfers, n_groups * group_size
letting golfers be n_groups * group_size

$ assign[g,w]: the group (0-based, from 0 to n_groups-1) of golfer g (indices 1-based) in week w (indices 1-based)
find assign : matrix indexed by [int(1..golfers), int(1..n_weeks)] of int(0..n_groups-1)

such that
$ each week, every group has exactly group_size golfers
forAll w : int(1..n_weeks) . forAll k : int(0..n_groups-1) . (sum g : int(1..golfers) . toInt(assign[g,w] = k)) = group_size,
$ no two golfers play in the same group more than once: for each pair of golfers, the number of weeks they share a group is at most 1
forAll g1 : int(1..golfers) . forAll g2 : int(1..golfers) . (g1 < g2) -> (sum w : int(1..n_weeks) . toInt(assign[g1,w] = assign[g2,w])) <= 1
